## BSIM4 Tests

The tests files `bsim/test/b4_*.gc` are adopted from on the official BSIM4
release from UC Berkeley group, available at [1]. The syntax has been changed
to Verilog-like and they need porting to Verilog.

Since the latest version BSIM4 version (4.8.3) does not include official benchmarks, we use test cases and reference data from the previous release (4.8.1), available here: https://www.bsim.berkeley.edu/BSIM4/BSIM4_4.8.1_20170215.tar.gz.

The official Berkley testbench includes static DC, AC and Transient test cases. To run all tests, execute

$ make check

within the `bsim/BSIM483` directory. Simulation results are automatically diffed against the reference output files located in `bsim/BSIM483/ref` directory.  

## Ratings

Each test result is assigned a rating reflecting its level of agreement with the official benchmark output files `bsim/BSIM483/benchamrk/*.out`. 

+ Basic sanity check passed - result appears physically reasonable
++ Good qualitative match with benchmark 
+++ Quantative match up to numerical tolerance 

### DC sweeps 

b4_test1.gc  +++
b4_test2.gc  +++ 
b4_test3.gc  +++
